```

This function iterates over each number in the input list `nums`. It checks if the number is greater than 10. If it is, it converts the number to a string to easily access the first and last digits. It then checks if both the first and last digits are odd using the helper function `is_odd_digit`. If both conditions are met, it increments the count. Finally, it returns the count of such numbers.
